  <!--HOME_INSIGHTS_START-->
<section id="insights" style="background:var(--ivory-deep);"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div class="eyebrow">Notes from the region</div><h2>Insights.</h2><p>Market intelligence on Caribbean citizenship, real estate and the families repositioning capital here.</p></div><div class="carousel" role="group" aria-label="Insights"><button class="carousel-nav carousel-prev" type="button" aria-label="Scroll back"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15.4 4.2 7.6 12l7.8 7.8 1.4-1.4L10.4 12l6.4-6.4z"/></svg></button><div class="carousel-track" role="group" aria-label="Insights"><a class="ins" data-cat="Citizenship by Investment" href="/articles/is-the-golden-age-of-caribbean-citizenship-ending" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/aerial-villa-resort-above-caribbean-hillside-town-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/aerial-villa-resort-above-caribbean-hillside-town-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/aerial-villa-resort-above-caribbean-hillside-town-1200w.webp 1200w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/aerial-villa-resort-above-caribbean-hillside-town-1500w.webp 1500w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/aerial-villa-resort-above-caribbean-hillside-town-1500w.jpg" alt="An aerial view of a villa resort with two lap pools and palm-shaded lawns above a Caribbean hillside town" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1500" height="1125"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Citizenship by Investment</div><h3>Is the Golden Age of Caribbean Citizenship Ending?</h3><p>Prices doubled, scrutiny is up, and a real regulator now exists. Is Caribbean CBI dying — or finally growing up? My honest read on what's happening.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Wealth & Tax" href="/articles/which-us-states-hnw-americans-are-leaving" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/traveller-with-suitcase-crossing-transit-plaza-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/traveller-with-suitcase-crossing-transit-plaza-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/traveller-with-suitcase-crossing-transit-plaza-1200w.webp 1200w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/traveller-with-suitcase-crossing-transit-plaza-1600w.webp 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/traveller-with-suitcase-crossing-transit-plaza-1600w.jpg" alt="A traveller pulling a wheeled suitcase across a cobblestone plaza beside a modern glass and steel transit hall" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1880" height="1253"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Wealth & Tax</div><h3>Where Wealthy Americans Are Fleeing — and What's Next</h3><p>IRS data shows HNW Americans leaving California and New York for no-tax states like Florida and Texas — and why some then look offshore for a Plan B.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Real Estate" href="/articles/how-to-hold-caribbean-real-estate" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/windward-estate-villa-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/windward-estate-villa-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/windward-estate-villa-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/windward-estate-villa-1200w.jpg" alt="How to Hold Caribbean Real Estate: Your Name, a Company, or a Trust" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="750"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Real Estate</div><h3>How to Hold Caribbean Real Estate: Your Name, a Company, or a Trust</h3><p>Own name, company or trust: the choice decides what happens on your death, how easily you can sell, and how exposed the villa is. The trade-offs, set out.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Wealth & Tax" href="/articles/ec-dollar-peg-caribbean-currency-risk" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/uncut-sheet-banknotes-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/uncut-sheet-banknotes-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/uncut-sheet-banknotes-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/uncut-sheet-banknotes-1200w.jpg" alt="The EC Dollar Peg: Fifty Years Fixed, and What Would Have to Break It" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="800"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Wealth & Tax</div><h3>The EC Dollar Peg: Fifty Years Fixed, and What Would Have to Break It</h3><p>The EC dollar has sat at 2.70 since 1976, backed at 97%. What the peg protects, what would break it, and why Caribbean deals price in USD anyway.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Global Mobility" href="/articles/non-dom-leavers-one-year-on-the-data" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/hillside-harbour-town-yacht-marina-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/hillside-harbour-town-yacht-marina-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/hillside-harbour-town-yacht-marina-1200w.webp 1200w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/hillside-harbour-town-yacht-marina-1510w.webp 1510w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/hillside-harbour-town-yacht-marina-1510w.jpg" alt="An elevated view over a horseshoe-shaped harbour town on a green hillside, its marina filled with moored yachts and sailboats beside a docked cargo ship and dockside warehouses" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1510" height="1132"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Global Mobility</div><h3>Non-Dom Leavers, One Year On: What the Data Actually Shows</h3><p>A year after the non-dom regime ended, HMRC's figures show claimants down 1% and the tax take up 9%. What the exodus forecasts got wrong.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Wealth & Tax" href="/articles/feie-vs-foreign-tax-credit" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/two-travellers-walking-toward-jet-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/two-travellers-walking-toward-jet-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/two-travellers-walking-toward-jet-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/two-travellers-walking-toward-jet-1200w.jpg" alt="FEIE vs the Foreign Tax Credit: Why a Tax-Free Island Can Raise Your US Bill" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="800"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Wealth & Tax</div><h3>FEIE vs the Foreign Tax Credit: Why a Tax-Free Island Can Raise Your US Bill</h3><p>The FEIE and the Foreign Tax Credit are the two tools US expats use to cut tax. On a zero-tax island, one is a small shield and the other gives you nothing.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Real Estate" href="/articles/dominica-geothermal-power-investment-case" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/soufriere-hills-volcano-rising-green-hillsides-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/soufriere-hills-volcano-rising-green-hillsides-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/soufriere-hills-volcano-rising-green-hillsides-1000w.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/soufriere-hills-volcano-rising-green-hillsides-1000w.jpg" alt="Dominica’s Geothermal Plant Is Running. What Cheap Power Does to the Investment Case" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="563"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Real Estate</div><h3>Dominica’s Geothermal Plant Is Running. What Cheap Power Does to the Investment Case</h3><p>Dominica’s 10 MW geothermal plant entered commercial operation in August 2026. What it does to electricity bills and villa running costs.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Wealth & Tax" href="/articles/section-1031-exchange-foreign-property" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/tax-withholding-form-hundred-dollar-notes-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/tax-withholding-form-hundred-dollar-notes-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/tax-withholding-form-hundred-dollar-notes-1000w.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/tax-withholding-form-hundred-dollar-notes-1000w.jpg" alt="A US tax withholding form and hundred-dollar notes lying on a desk calendar" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="563"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Wealth & Tax</div><h3>Section 1031 Stops at the Border: Selling US Property to Buy in the Caribbean</h3><p>A 1031 exchange cannot move US property into a Caribbean one. The rule, the one Caribbean exception, why Puerto Rico is not it, and what the tax costs.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Real Estate" href="/articles/dominica-international-airport" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/which-caribbean-islands-are-actually-a-direct-flight-home-hero-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/which-caribbean-islands-are-actually-a-direct-flight-home-hero-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/which-caribbean-islands-are-actually-a-direct-flight-home-hero-1024w.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/which-caribbean-islands-are-actually-a-direct-flight-home-hero-1024w.jpg" alt="Dominica’s New International Airport: What It Changes, and When" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="683"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Real Estate</div><h3>Dominica’s New International Airport: What It Changes, and When</h3><p>Dominica’s international airport at Wesley, on track for 2027: the contract, the construction numbers, and what it does to property values.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a><a class="ins" data-cat="Citizenship by Investment" href="/articles/dominica-vs-grenada-citizenship" style="display:block;color:inherit;"><div class="ph"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/citizenship-by-investment-caribbean-overview-part-2-hero-480w.webp 480w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/citizenship-by-investment-caribbean-overview-part-2-hero-800w.webp 800w, https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/citizenship-by-investment-caribbean-overview-part-2-hero-1000w.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) calc(100vw - 64px), 361px"><img src="https://www.danmerriam.com/assets/articles-img/citizenship-by-investment-caribbean-overview-part-2-hero-1000w.jpg" alt="Dominica or Grenada? The Cheapest Passport Against the E-2 One" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="562"></picture></div><div class="ib"><div class="cat">Citizenship by Investment</div><h3>Dominica or Grenada? The Cheapest Passport Against the E-2 One</h3><p>Grenada’s E-2 treaty and China access against Dominica’s price and speed, plus the three-year domicile rule that changes the E-2 pitch.</p><span class="rm">Read &#8594;</span></div></a></div><button class="carousel-nav carousel-next" type="button" aria-label="Scroll forward"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8.6 4.2 7.2 5.6 13.6 12l-6.4 6.4 1.4 1.4L16.4 12z"/></svg></button></div><div style="text-align:center;margin-top:40px;"><a class="btn btn-line-dark" href="/articles/">All Articles</a></div></div></section>
